@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/releases/414551633","assets_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/releases/414551633/assets","upload_url":"https://uploads.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/releases/414551633/assets{?name,label}","html_url":"https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/releases/tag/v0.64.0","id":414551633,"author":{"login":"marten-seemann","id":1478487,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Nzg0ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1478487?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann","html_url":"https://github.com/marten-seemann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDOA1D2R84YtY5R","tag_name":"v0.64.0","target_commitish":"master","name":"v0.64.0","draft":false,"immutable":true,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-10-16T04:49:49Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T04:54:53Z","published_at":"2026-10-16T04:54:53Z","assets":[],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/tarball/v0.64.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/zipball/v0.64.0","body":"\r\nThis release improves congestion control and performance, especially on paths with packet reordering:\r\n\r\n* Slow-start pacing now uses twice the estimated bandwidth, allowing the sending rate to double each RTT: [#5882](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5882)\r\n* Application-data loss detection now disables packet-threshold detection after a spurious loss, avoiding repeated unnecessary retransmissions caused by packet reordering: [#5905](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5905)\r\n* Application-data loss detection now uses an adaptive time threshold that increases after spurious losses, allowing more time for reordered packets to arrive: [#5925](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5925)\r\n* The congestion controller now restores its congestion window and recovery state after a reduction caused entirely by spurious packet loss: [#5923](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5923)\r\n\r\n## Notable Fixes\r\n\r\n* Congestion recovery now respects send order across Initial, Handshake and application-data packets, fixing incorrect recovery decisions caused by comparing packet numbers from different spaces: [#5920](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5920)\r\n* Connections now fall back to 1200-byte Initial packets on `EMSGSIZE` when `Config.InitialPacketSize` is unset, allowing handshakes over paths with smaller MTUs: [#5911](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5911)\r\n* Oversized packets are now rejected before serialization, including Initial packets with excessively large address-validation tokens: [#5937](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5937)\r\n* Path MTU discovery now restarts correctly after connection migration and NAT rebinding: [#5887](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5887)\r\n* Servers now retry unanswered PATH_CHALLENGEs with exponential backoff as more packets arrive on the candidate path, preventing path validation from stalling when a challenge is acknowledged but no PATH_RESPONSE arrives: [#5930](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5930)\r\n* Servers now continue responding to PATH_CHALLENGEs on existing candidate paths when the candidate path limit is reached: [#5929](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5929)\r\n* Writes after closing a `SendStream` or `Stream` now return `quic.ErrStreamClosed`, which is also used as the stream context's cancellation cause: [#5885](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5885)\r\n* `Conn.SendDatagram` now returns the connection's close error after shutdown, instead of accepting datagrams that will be silently dropped: [#5880](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5880)\r\n* http3: `SendDatagram` now immediately returns an error after the stream's send side closes, including after STOP_SENDING or connection shutdown: [#5884](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5884)\r\n* http3: request header, response header and trailer buffers now grow as data arrives, avoiding large allocations based solely on a peer's advertised HEADERS frame length: [#5886](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5886)\r\n* Spurious losses are now detected when an ACK only acknowledges packets previously declared lost: [#5895](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5895)\r\n* Spurious losses are now detected when ACKs arrive out of order: [#5900](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5900)\r\n* Path migration now clears the old path's loss history, preventing stale spurious-loss reports and recovery adjustments: [#5903](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5903)\r\n* MTU and path probes no longer trigger spurious-loss reports or adaptive loss-recovery changes: [#5906](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5906)\r\n\r\n## Notable Changes\r\n\r\n* `ConnectionStats` now exposes `CongestionWindow`, reporting the local sender's congestion window on the active network path in bytes: [#5901](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5901)\r\n* `http3.Stream` and `http3.RequestStream` now expose `QlogTrace`, allowing applications to add events to the underlying connection's qlog trace: [#5935](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5935)\r\n* `http3/qlog.RedactHeaders` allows applications to redact HTTP/3 header and trailer values, including pseudo-headers, before they are written to qlog: [#5932](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5932)\r\n* qlog: locally dropped QUIC datagrams are now recorded with `quic:datagram_dropped`, including drops caused by a full receive buffer or an oversized outgoing datagram: [#5907](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5907)\r\n* qlog: `quic:recovery_parameters_set` now records initial recovery parameters and changes to loss-detection thresholds, including resets after path migration: [#5926](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5926)\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* return an error from Conn.SendDatagram when the connection is closed by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5880\r\n* http3: fail SendDatagram as soon as the send side is closed by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5884\r\n* use ErrStreamClosed instead of context.Canceled for closed streams by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5885\r\n* congestion: pass the pacing rate explicitly to the pacer by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5881\r\n* congestion: increase slow start pacing factor to 2 by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5882\r\n* http3: grow header block buffers as data arrives by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5886\r\n* ackhandler: use a fixed cap for tracked lost packets by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5888\r\n* ackhandler: detect spurious loss when only lost packets are ACKed by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5895\r\n* ackhandler: avoid floating point math for time threshold calculations by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5896\r\n* ackhandler: move MaxAckDelay constant from the protocol package by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5892\r\n* ackhandler: don’t store MaxAckDelay on the appDataReceivedPacketTracker by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5893\r\n* congestion: move MinPacingDelay constant from the protocol package by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5889\r\n* handshake: move the KeyUpdateInterval from the protocol package by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5891\r\n* ackhandler: detect spurious losses in reordered ACKs by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5900\r\n* move 0-RTT queue constants from the protocol package by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5890\r\n* remove the fixed size cap on post-handshake CRYPTO frames by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5902\r\n* ackhandler: clear lost packet history on path migration by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5903\r\n* ackhandler: move packet number skipping consts from the protocol package by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5904\r\n* expose the sender's congestion window in ConnectionStats by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5901\r\n* ackhandler: disable packet-threshold loss detection on spurious losses by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5905\r\n* ackhandler: exclude MTU and path probes from lost packet tracking by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5906\r\n* fix MTU probing after path changes by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5887\r\n* qlog locally dropped QUIC datagrams by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5907\r\n* ci: bump CodSpeedHQ/action from 5.2.1 to 5.4.0 by @dependabot[bot] in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5912\r\n* ci: update golangci-lint to v2.14.0 by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5919\r\n* utils: use uint32 for random number generation by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5916\r\n* ackhandler: use a uint32 countdown for packet number skipping by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5917\r\n* introduce a dedicated type for packet number spaces by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5921\r\n* use packet numbers from a single packet number space by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5920\r\n* restore congestion control state after spurious packet loss by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5923\r\n* ackhandler: increase the time threshold after spurious losses by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5925\r\n* fall back to 1200 bytes initial packet size on EMSGSIZE by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5911\r\n* qlog initial recovery parameters and loss threshold updates by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5926\r\n* README: link OSS-Fuzz badge to the introspector by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5928\r\n* http3/qlog: implement redacting of header fields by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5932\r\n* http3: expose the connection's qlog trace on streams by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5935\r\n* reject oversized packets before serialization by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5937\r\n* only enforce the candidate path limit for new paths by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5929\r\n* retry server path challenges with exponential backoff by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5930\r\n\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/compare/v0.63.0...v0.64.0","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/releases/414551633/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"mentions_count":2}
