+{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/releases/432146335","assets_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/releases/432146335/assets","upload_url":"https://uploads.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/releases/432146335/assets{?name,label}","html_url":"https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/releases/tag/v0.65.0","id":432146335,"author":{"login":"marten-seemann","id":1478487,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0Nzg0ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1478487?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann","html_url":"https://github.com/marten-seemann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marten-seemann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDOA1D2R84Zwgef","tag_name":"v0.65.0","target_commitish":"master","name":"v0.65.0","draft":false,"immutable":true,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-11-03T01:12:34Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T01:14:15Z","published_at":"2026-11-03T01:14:15Z","assets":[],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/tarball/v0.65.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quic-go/quic-go/zipball/v0.65.0","body":"This release updates qlog to the latest IETF drafts, adds explicit stream credit release, and fixes a number of HTTP/3 and connection migration bugs.\r\n\r\n* With `Config.RequireStreamCreditRelease`, completed streams count towards the incoming stream limit until the application calls `ReleaseStreamCredit`: [#5981](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5981), [#5982](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5982)\r\n* qlog: events now follow draft-ietf-quic-qlog-quic-events-14 and draft-ietf-quic-qlog-h3-events-14: [#6120](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6120)\r\n\r\n## Breaking Changes\r\n\r\n* http3: `HTTPStreamer.HTTPStream` now returns `(*Stream, error)`, and no longer sends an implicit 200 response: [#5988](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5988), [#5994](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5994)\r\n\r\n## Notable Fixes\r\n\r\n* QUIC v2 key updates now use the correct `quicv2 ku` label: [#5973](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5973)\r\n* Connections using zero-length connection IDs no longer stop receiving packets after version negotiation: [#6129](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6129)\r\n* Switching paths now uses a new connection ID, fixing servers that kept sending to the old address after repeated NAT rebindings: [#6015](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6015)\r\n* Clients now send PATH_RESPONSE on the path the PATH_CHALLENGE was received on: [#5980](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5980)\r\n* `Path.Probe` now succeeds on an already validated path: [#6019](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6019)\r\n* Reordered and retransmitted NEW_CONNECTION_ID frames are now handled correctly: [#6009](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6009), [#6007](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6007)\r\n* DATAGRAM frames no longer starve ACKs, control frames and retransmissions: [#5970](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5970)\r\n* `CancelRead` now unblocks `Read` and `Peek` after receiving RESET_STREAM_AT: [#6022](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6022)\r\n* `TryWriteAll` no longer copies queued data quadratically: [#6042](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6042), [#6043](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6043)\r\n* http3: canceling the first request to a host no longer cancels the shared dial: [#6132](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6132)\r\n* http3: bodies shorter than the announced Content-Length now fail with `io.ErrUnexpectedEOF`: [#5913](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5913)\r\n* http3: Content-Length is no longer added to 204 and 304 responses, and is now sent for requests with `http.NoBody`: [#6032](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6032), [#6029](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6029)\r\n* http3: response writes that fail partway (e.g. on a write deadline) no longer corrupt the stream: [#5993](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5993), [#6002](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6002), [#6001](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6001), [#6003](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6003)\r\n* http3: canceling an Extended CONNECT request now interrupts waiting for SETTINGS: [#6020](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6020)\r\n* qlog fixes:\r\n  * incorrect or missing values for transport parameters, packet numbers, congestion metrics, timers, connection IDs and lengths: [#6050](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6050), [#6054](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6054), [#6059](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6059), [#6060](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6060), [#6074](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6074), [#6077](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6077), [#6091](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6091), [#6023](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6023), [#5969](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5969)\r\n  * stateless resets are logged as remote closures: [#6063](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6063)\r\n  * concurrently recorded events are written in order: [#5956](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5956)\r\n  * traces of connections abandoned after version negotiation are closed: [#6130](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6130)\r\n  * http3: traces no longer close before all events are recorded: [#6090](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6090), [#6083](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6083), [#6041](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6041)\r\n\r\n## Notable Changes\r\n\r\n* Multiple DATAGRAM frames are now packed into a single packet: [#5961](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5961), [#5960](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5960)\r\n* qlog: new `connection_state_updated` and HTTP/3 `stream_type_set` events, and tuples for path probing and migration: [#6111](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6111), [#6113](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6113), [#5977](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5977), [#5979](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5979)\r\n* qlog: `qlog.RedactIPs` redacts IP addresses and ports: [#5943](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5943)\r\n* qlog: HTTP/3 connections now use `qlog.DefaultConnectionTracer`; `http3/qlog.DefaultConnectionTracer` is removed: [#5966](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5966)\r\n* Reduced allocations during the handshake: [#6096](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6096), [#6093](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6093), [#6098](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6098), [#6097](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6097), [#6095](https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6095)\r\n\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* ci: bump CodSpeedHQ/action from 5.4.0 to 5.5.0 by @dependabot[bot] in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5945\r\n* qlogwriter: fix ordering of concurrently recorded events by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5956\r\n* omit the length field of the last DATAGRAM frame in a packet by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5960\r\n* remove obsolete curve ID helpers from handshake tests by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5968\r\n* handshake: remove obsolete session ticket error workaround by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5967\r\n* pack multiple DATAGRAM frames into a packet by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5961\r\n* qlog: register event schemas on init, remove Trace.SupportsSchemas by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5966\r\n* qlog: support redacting IP addresses and ports by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5943\r\n* qlog: distinguish zero lengths from omitted lengths by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5969\r\n* prioritize control frames and retransmissions over DATAGRAM frames by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5970\r\n* handshake: fix the key update label for QUIC v2 by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5973\r\n* queue packets received on inactive client paths separately  by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5976\r\n* ci: bump docker/login-action from 4.6.0 to 4.7.0 by @dependabot[bot] in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5985\r\n* ci: bump CodSpeedHQ/action from 5.5.0 to 5.6.0 by @dependabot[bot] in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5984\r\n* allow the application to explicitly release stream credit by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5981\r\n* expose ReleaseStreamCredit on the ConnectionState by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5982\r\n* qlog: log tuples for client path probing and migration by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5977\r\n* qlog: log tuples for server path probing and migration by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5979\r\n* http3: don't send an implicit 200 response from HTTPStream by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5988\r\n* http3: fail writes on HTTPStream without a response header by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5989\r\n* http3: resume writing the response header after a partial write by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5993\r\n* http3: return an error from HTTPStream if sending the header fails by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5994\r\n* http3: return http.ErrHijacked from Write after HTTPStream by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5998\r\n* http3: only count written body bytes towards Content-Length by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6001\r\n* send client’s PATH_RESPONSE on the probed path by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/5980\r\n* http3: resume writing DATA frames after a partial write by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6002\r\n* http3: cancel incomplete responses instead of closing the stream by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6003\r\n* process Retire Prior To for every NEW_CONNECTION_ID frame by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6009\r\n* don't retire or reuse connection IDs on retransmitted NEW_CONNECTION_ID by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6007\r\n* unblock Read and Peek on CancelRead after receiving RESET_STREAM_AT by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6022\r\n* http3: stop waiting for SETTINGS when Extended CONNECT is canceled by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6020\r\n* qlog: fix swapped connection IDs of received Version Negotiation packets by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6023\r\n* fix validation of Version Negotiation packets by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6024\r\n* allow probing a path again after it was validated by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6019\r\n* drop Handshake packets sent to the client's Initial connection ID by @marten-seemann in https://github.com/quic-go/quic-go/pull/6021\r\n* use a new connection ID and retire the old one when swi